Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:00:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: stop the staggered fast scroller thumb from jumping

The thumb used the average height of whichever cells were on screen. Mixing
3:2 and 2:3 cells changes that average as the window moves, so the thumb
twitched. Heights are now kept by index for the life of the grid state.
Offset and range sum those heights, using the running average where a cell
has not been measured yet, and full-line rows are left out. The content
padding before the list is still added to the offset, as the previous
estimate did, so a resting list reports offset 0.

Harmony-only: same staggered-grid scroller estimate as the one being added on Anikku; Animeko does not use this scroller.
